. Extended\n  the gate to `from_zone == STACK` and added\n  `SpellPutIntoGraveyardReplacementEvent`, passed by `_resolve_spell` for\n  instants/sorceries. Limitation: fdn_48-style local `_counter_spell` moves the\n  countered card to the graveyard directly, bypassing replacements — a spell\n  countered while Archaic's exile-instead applies still goes to the graveyard.\n- sos_1: the exile-instead replacement is one-shot (unregisters after applying)\n  since it binds to that cast of the spell, not the card forever.\n- sos_257: restricted mana in `ManaPool` supports exactly one restriction kind\n  (\"instant_or_sorcery\") — a deliberate card-local limitation. When allowed,\n  restricted mana is consumed before unrestricted mana (deterministic; always\n  at least as good for the player). `cast_spell` enables it for\n  instant/sorcery spells only; ability costs never use it.\n- sos_57: \"mana spent to cast that spell\" = amount actually paid after cost\n  reductions — `cast_spell` now stamps `card.mana_spent = effective_cost.cmc`\n  (0 for free casts). The Wizard check happens when the delayed trigger fires\n  (per TODO), and the trigger is one-shot whether or not a Wizard was present.\n  Limitation: \"your next main phase\" = next *precombat* main (no\n  postcombat-main event exists in the engine).\n- sos_257: the {5} animation mutates in place and updates the\n  original-characteristics snapshot, since \"it becomes a creature\" has no\n  duration — the new identity is the permanent baseline.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":27,"oldLines":6,"newStart":27,"newLines":16,"lines":["   (per TODO), and the trigger is one-shot whether or not a Wizard was present.","   Limitation: \"your next main phase\" = next *precombat* main (no","   postcombat-main event exists in the engine).","+- sos_13: TODO suggested a `register_triggers` ETB + free cast; the engine","+  fires `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent` *before* registering the entering","+  card's own triggers (ordering pinned by engine_tests), so the ETB effect is","+  implemented in `on_resolve` like fdn_12. RULEBOOK 722.3c says the prepared","+  copy is \"cast\" (normally) — so `cast_prepared_spell` pays the copy's {W}","+  cost explicitly, then uses `cast_spell_free` from exile as the mechanism.","+  The prepared-creature count includes the entering Emeritus (+1) since","+  on_resolve runs just before it reaches the battlefield. The copy is exposed","+  via a card-local `cast_prepared_spell(game)` method (the engine has no","+  \"castable from exile\" action seam)."," - sos_257: the {5} animation mutates in place and updates the","   original-characteristics snapshot, since \"it becomes a creature\" has no","   duration — the new identity is the permanent baseline."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
