eplacements — a spell\n  countered while Archaic's exile-instead applies still goes to the graveyard.\n- sos_1: the exile-instead replacement is one-shot (unregisters after applying)\n  since it binds to that cast of the spell, not the card forever.\n- sos_257: restricted mana in `ManaPool` supports exactly one restriction kind\n  (\"instant_or_sorcery\") — a deliberate card-local limitation. When allowed,\n  restricted mana is consumed before unrestricted mana (deterministic; always\n  at least as good for the player). `cast_spell` enables it for\n  instant/sorcery spells only; ability costs never use it.\n- sos_57: \"mana spent to cast that spell\" = amount actually paid after cost\n  reductions — `cast_spell` now stamps `card.mana_spent = effective_cost.cmc`\n  (0 for free casts). The Wizard check happens when the delayed trigger fires\n  (per TODO), and the trigger is one-shot whether or not a Wizard was present.\n  Limitation: \"your next main phase\" = next *precombat* main (no\n  postcombat-main event exists in the engine).\n- sos_13: TODO suggested a `register_triggers` ETB + free cast; the engine\n  fires `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent` *before* registering the entering\n  card's own triggers (ordering pinned by engine_tests), so the ETB effect is\n  implemented in `on_resolve` like fdn_12. RULEBOOK 722.3c says the prepared\n  copy is \"cast\" (normally) — so `cast_prepared_spell` pays the copy's {W}\n  cost explicitly, then uses `cast_spell_free` from exile as the mechanism.\n  The prepared-creature count includes the entering Emeritus (+1) since\n  on_resolve runs just before it reaches the battlefield. The copy is exposed\n  via a card-local `cast_prepared_spell(game)` method (the engine has no\n  \"castable from exile\" action seam).\n- sos_257: the {5} animation mutates in place and updates the\n  original-characteristics snapshot, since \"it becomes a creature\" has no\n  duration — the new identity is the permanent baseline.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":5,"newStart":1,"newLines":13,"lines":[" # Key decisions log"," ","+- sos_97: surveil keeps non-binned cards in their existing library order (no","+  reorder choice) — local limitation. Skip-turns consumed at the turn handoff","+  in `advance_phase` (interacts with the extra-turns queue: skipped player's","+  pending extra turns are also consumed by skips, simplest consistent rule).","+  `game.rng` added to `GameState` for deterministic coin flips; loyalty","+  ability targets are read from `self.chosen_targets`, which tests set","+  directly (the engine only populates it for spells).","+"," - E1: `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` is fired from **both** `cast_spell` and","   `cast_spell_free` — a spell cast without paying its mana cost is still","   \"cast\" per the rules (601.2), so casualty/pump triggers must see free"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
